133
00:06:57,390 --> 00:06:59,890
somatic dysfunctions we're
talking about a preference

134
00:06:59,890 --> 00:07:02,310
of either medial or lateral
glide of the proximal

135
00:07:02,310 --> 00:07:05,670
ulna. Now, these are
accessory rocking motions of

136
00:07:05,670 --> 00:07:08,830
the proximal ulna on the
trochlea of the humerus.

137
00:07:09,270 --> 00:07:12,440
We can also induce these
motions by supinating and

138
00:07:12,440 --> 00:07:14,830
pronating the forearm,
which I'll cover on the next

139
00:07:14,830 --> 00:07:18,430
slide. So what you'll observe
