389
00:21:29,390 --> 00:21:32,910
And so if we have an ulno
-humeral abduction somatic

390
00:21:32,910 --> 00:21:35,290
dysfunction, the medial
glide, which is shown by

391
00:21:35,290 --> 00:21:37,690
this black arrow here, is
the preferred motion at

392
00:21:37,690 --> 00:21:40,690
the proximal ulna, which
then likely translates

393
00:21:40,690 --> 00:21:43,690
to a preferred lateral
glide of the distal radius,

394
00:21:43,690 --> 00:21:47,150
and so if you were to find
an ulno-humeral abduction

395
00:21:47,150 --> 00:21:50,330
somatic dysfunction,
you would likely find an

396
00:21:51,050 --> 00:21:53,830
adduction radiocarpal
joint somatic dysfunction.

397
00:21:53,830 --> 00:21:56,570
And the reverse is
true too, where if

398
00:21:56,570 --> 00:21:58,750
you were to find a
radiocarpal adduction

399
00:21:58,750 --> 00:22:01,410
somatic dysfunction,
you would likely find an

400
00:22:01,410 --> 00:22:04,090
